[2022-03-29T10:23:15.000+0000 | Aleksey Midenkov]
{quote}It is unclear to me how the proposed idea would work on incomplete transactions that were recovered after the server was killed and restarted. A quick look in the code suggests that trx_t::mod_tables are only being updated for recovered transactions that are in the XA PREPARE state (and will remain in that state until an explicit commit or rollback statement).{quote}

In this bug we solve stale data in TABLE object. On server restart of course any data is reloaded.

---

[2022-03-31T10:50:54.000+0000 | Aleksey Midenkov]
{quote}The InnoDB dict_table_t actually corresponds to TABLE_SHARE in the SQL layer and not TABLE. The TABLE is a table handle or a cursor, which would roughly correspond to row_prebuilt_t in InnoDB.{quote}

You right. Moreover lifetimes of TABLE_SHARE and dict_table_t are independent by design. So we have to acquire TABLE_SHARE each time we need it in InnoDB.

---

[2022-04-01T06:16:21.000+0000 | Aleksey Midenkov]
Then the simplest solution is to process partitions each time from start for LIMIT in vers_set_hist_part().

